marta: Heads-up — found a confusing copy/paste trap in the JS sample app README (packages/examples/sample-app/README.md). The async fetch snippet reassigns the API key inside the handler which can lead to people accidentally committing a temp token or triggering our retry loop. Example from line ~42:
```js
// BAD: reassigning process.env inside request handler
app.post('/send', async (req, res) => {
  process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY = req.body.api_key // copied from tutorial
  try {
    const out = await client.generate({ prompt: req.body.prompt })
    res.send(out)
  } catch (e) {
    // retry logic lives in runtime, ends up spamming if key is invalid
    res.status(500).send('err')
  }
})
```
This is exactly the kind of snippet drift that causes onboarding friction.

ajay: oh no. yeah that inline `process.env` assignment is a bad pattern — explains why some new users saw repeated 401s + high retry counts in telemetry. we should not show mutating env in examples. quick fix: read from env once outside handler and pass into client constructor.

kevin: i noticed a similar pattern in the python quickstart earlier this month (docs/quickstarts/python.md) — they create a `client = Client(api_key=os.getenv("REDWOOD_API_KEY"))` but then later show `os.environ["REDWOOD_API_KEY"] = ...` in a test snippet. we should audit all quickstarts.

emily: thanks for flagging @marta. can someone open a docs PR to: 1) replace the problematic snippet with a safer pattern, 2) add a short note in the README about not embedding tokens in code, 3) add a tiny unit that runs snippets in CI (snippet-tests) so we catch copy/paste bugs?

ajay: i'll open the PR in docs repo and include the snippet-tests change. putting up a draft now: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5123 — it updates the JS sample to:
```js
// GOOD: load once at startup and never reassign
const API_KEY = process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: API_KEY })
app.post('/send', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const out = await client.generate({ prompt: req.body.prompt })
    res.send(out)
  } catch (e) {
    // surface friendly error, do NOT mutate env or retry client construction here
    console.error('generation error', e.message)
    res.status(500).send({ error: 'internal' })
  }
})
```

docs-bot: Draft PR 5123 created by ajay — preview URL: https://deploy-preview.example.com/docs/5123 (build queued) :white_check_mark:

ci-bot: snippet-tests failed on staging for commit a1f2b3: `sample-app README snippet: exec error: EACCES` — looks like our snippet harness needs an environment shim for network calls. logs: `Error: spawn /usr/bin/node EACCES`.

ajay: thanks — i'll push a follow-up to the PR to update the harness to skip networked calls and use a mocked client for CI-run snippets. also adding a short doc comment advising people to use ephemeral tokens not to commit.

kevin: can we also add a linter rule in the devex docs repo to detect `process.env.SOMETHING =` patterns in markdown fenced code blocks? even a grep-based CI check would help.

emily: yes — action items: 1) ajay to land docs PR 5123 with fix + harness update (target EOD), 2) kevin to propose a grep-based CI check in docs CI (PR in infra repo), 3) marta to scan quickstarts for similar anti-patterns (prefill list below). Please add owners to the PR descriptions. I'll follow up in the weekly docs sync.

marta: adding the quick list: packages/examples/sample-app/README.md, docs/quickstarts/python.md, docs/quickstarts/node.md — i'll do a quick pass and post findings. thanks everyone :raised_hands:
